 them to make water turn to steam to  turn a turbine to power a generator okay  now the advantages of fossil fuels it's  first of all they are really reliable  they're a reliable source currently to  produce a lot of electricity to to give  electricity for everyone across across  the nation the other good thing about  them is they can be used to meet energy  demand so if there's a sudden demand for  more energy we can just burn more of the  fossil fuels in order to produce more  energy they also compared to lots of  other types of of energy generation  they're comparatively cheap to build and  to run so those are the benefits of  fossil fuels now there are lots and lots  of of negative of disadvantages of  fossil fuels as well because when you  burn the fossil fuels you're releasing  lots of harmful gases one is carbon  dioxide that could lead to global  warming there's another video to talk  that talks more about this particular  pollutant as well as this pollutant not  carbon dioxide but sulfur dioxide which  can cause acid rain again there's  another video it talks about these  effects in much more detail also if  you're using oil there could be oil  spillages which can be extremely  detrimental to animals such as bird such  as Birds so you can be completely  covered with the oil and can lead to the  deaths of of lots and lots of wildlife  and the other big negative thing about  fossil fuels is they will one day run  out because they are non-renewable they  cannot be replenished as we go so those  that's basically an overview of fossil  fuels now the other type of  non-renewable energy source is nuclear  power so instead of using fossil fuels  we have these different these different  fuels called uranium or plutonium again  are non-renewable because once you've  used them they are they're gone we can't  replenish them so the way that these  work is basically we have large unstable  nuclei and when we fire neutrons at them  it causes the nuclei to split into  smaller daughter daughter nuclei and  also it releases lots and lots of energy  so this energy released from splitting  these uranium or plutonium nuclei can  then be used in a very similar way to  fossil fuels to heat up water in a  boiler to then turn a turbine to  generate electricity in a generator so  what are the advantages of nuclear power  now compared to fossil fuels they really  produce low levels of co2 because unlike  burning the fossil fuels splitting these  atoms these nuclei does not release lots  of carbon dioxide also they can produce  a large amount of electricity so a  relatively small massive of these of  these substances uranium or plutonium  releases a lot of energy now the really  negative sides about nuclear power is  first of all it's extremely expensive to  build a nuclear power plant and to  decommission one after it's been built  but probably the biggest problem with  nuclear energy is it produces nuclear  waste  now nuclear waste is extremely harmful  to people and it stays dangerous for  thousands of years so a big problem is  thinking what to actually do with this  nuclear waste once it's been created  so that guys is basically an overview of  non-renewable energy thank you
 

